{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/370969-a-quick-question-prometheans-and-aura-detection","id":370969,"title":"A Quick Question: Prometheans and Aura-detection","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-15T07:04:00-08:00","id":370969,"title":"A Quick Question: Prometheans and Aura-detection","content":"I did a bit of reading and googling, but came up empty: do Prometheans have an aura, and what does it look like (i.e. Vampires are pale, Mages &quot;sparkle&quot;, etc.). My group is sort of gearing up for having our first Promethean character and we're not terribly well-versed in the splat yet. At best guess, I'd assume that their Aura might look human, but visually disjointed with the body -- some areas of the aura overlap with the body, some aren't connected, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T08:20:07-08:00","id":371053,"title":"","content":"Conveniently, Prometheans have an Aura Sight transmutation, so their book does in fact address this. Your suggestion is also excellent, and I'd stress that auras are probably the most interesting when they're a bit subjective and vary in perception from case to case. The book's brief description is &quot;fiery aura,&quot; which is to say, something of the Divine Fire that is stolen to animate a Promethean in place of a human soul can be perceived, harsh and uncomfortable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T08:49:46-08:00","id":371087,"title":"","content":"Thanks! Seems like you're helpful on whichever subforum I go to. Aura Perception is probably amongst my favorite abilities overall; I was rather sad when Vampires lost it in Second Edition (though their new Auspex is exciting in it's own right).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T09:06:47-08:00","id":371101,"title":"","content":"It is my nature to remember all kinds of niche facts and disgorge them at will. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I feel like vampires essentially still have the same ability they had before; it's simply presented with a different emphasis, as less of a one-size-fits-all psychic visual gloss, and more of a, well... uncanny perception. If you like the old Aura Perception, then I'd lean on the way that the Beast communicates its intuition through synesthetic hallucinations. Combining with the idea that auras are a little subjective and vary some, a vampire using Uncanny Perception can easily be portrayed as perceiving auric visions like those of Aura Perception, metaphorically expressive of those the vampire examines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T09:14:42-08:00","id":371105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/370969-a-quick-question-prometheans-and-aura-detection#post370969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At best guess, I'd assume that their Aura might look human, but visually disjointed with the body -- some areas of the aura overlap with the body, some aren't connected, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am also going to say this is an awesome idea!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"ht